WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.795
JAMIE: Unless the external review piece
has teeth. And we genuinely don't know

00:00:02.795 --> 00:00:05.589
JAMIE: yet if it does.

00:00:05.699 --> 00:00:09.888
ALEX: There's a continuity thread here
worth naming. Two days ago we were

00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:14.077
ALEX: debating whether AI safety should
be enforced through infrastructure-level
containment or executive-level

00:00:14.077 --> 00:00:18.265
ALEX: political accountability. This
accord is squarely in the executive-
political-accountability camp. And the

00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:22.454
ALEX: GitHub story we just covered is a
very concrete example of what

00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:26.643
ALEX: infrastructure-level failure looks
like in practice.

00:00:26.753 --> 00:00:30.572
RUFUS: The accord addresses the frontier
model risk — the GPT-6 class systems.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:34.392
RUFUS: It doesn't address the thirteen
thousand images sitting in public
repositories because

00:00:34.392 --> 00:00:38.211
RUFUS: a coding agent had the wrong
OAuth scope.
